  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Number of Radial nodes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Number of angular&nbsp;nodes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math></p><p>Where,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Azimuthal</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>quantum</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>principal</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>quantum</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> orbital, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> orbital the number of&nbsp;Radial nodes=<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>=1</p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> orbital the number of Angular nodes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>Thus, the number of radial and angular nodes in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> orbital are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p>",
